00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:50.440
Yes, the torture thing. I've read your book, which is wonderful by the way.

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:56.440
I love that you mention that as a leading nation that other nations look up to,

00:15:56.440 --> 00:16:00.440
we as a so-called civilized society should have the highest standards

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:06.440
when it comes to our behavior in times of war as well as in times of peace, obviously.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:11.440
We really need to be that beacon of hope that the rest of the world wants us to be.

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:14.440
We need to be examples for other countries.

00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:19.440
We point and print a couple of times that not only do we have a torture law in this country

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:22.440
called the Federal Torture Act which bans torture

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:27.440
and which actually goes to the trouble of defining torture and banning it

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:34.000
And not only are we signatories to the United Nations Convention Against Torture, but we

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:37.560
actually wrote the United Nations Convention Against Torture.

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:44.320
So then for us to go out and do exactly what we've been urging other countries to not do

