00:37:18.000 --> 00:37:22.000
We found a file folder full of telephone bills,

00:37:22.000 --> 00:37:26.000
and the telephone bills showed hundreds of phone calls

00:37:26.000 --> 00:37:29.000
to numbers all around the United States,

00:37:29.000 --> 00:37:32.000
Kansas City, Buffalo, Detroit, Atlanta,

00:37:32.000 --> 00:37:36.000
San Francisco, just all over the United States.

00:37:36.000 --> 00:37:40.000
And then those calls ended abruptly on September 10th, 2001.

00:37:40.000 --> 00:37:47.000
and then they began again slowly around September 16th so I informed the headquarters that we

00:37:47.000 --> 00:37:53.000
had found this and I thought obviously it was very significant so CIA said good catch

00:37:53.000 --> 00:37:57.000
it's an FBI issue so give the originals to the FBI.

00:37:57.000 --> 00:38:02.000
So I boxed up the originals I turned them over to the FBI and I went about my business.

00:38:02.000 --> 00:38:07.000
When I got back home to headquarters several months later I ran into an FBI agent

00:38:07.000 --> 00:38:09.800
an FBI agent with whom I had worked in Pakistan.

00:38:09.800 --> 00:38:11.560
And I said, hey, what ever happened

00:38:11.560 --> 00:38:14.040
with those Taliban and Fondos?

00:38:14.040 --> 00:38:16.520
And he said, oh, we haven't gone through them yet

00:38:16.520 --> 00:38:20.080
because we're having trouble identifying a Pashto translator.

00:38:20.080 --> 00:38:21.960
I said, a Pashto translator?

00:38:21.960 --> 00:38:24.080
Those Fondos were in English.

00:38:24.080 --> 00:38:25.440
That's how I knew what they were.

00:38:25.440 --> 00:38:27.000
I don't speak Pashto.

00:38:27.000 --> 00:38:29.640
Oh, he says, oh, our mistake.

00:38:29.640 --> 00:38:32.120
Colonel, okay, I thought, yeah, your mistake.

00:38:32.120 --> 00:38:34.400
These are presumably all Taliban recruits

00:38:34.400 --> 00:38:35.800
littered around America.

00:38:35.800 --> 00:38:42.800
They could have been legitimate consular calls, but I think more likely that they were, yeah,

00:38:42.800 --> 00:38:49.040
I mean, possible Taliban recruits, possible sleeper cells, possible terrorists just waiting

00:38:49.040 --> 00:38:50.040
to be activated.

00:38:50.040 --> 00:38:52.040
You don't know until you investigate.

00:38:52.040 --> 00:38:53.040
They didn't investigate.

00:38:53.040 --> 00:39:00.040
So another year and a half passes, and I resigned from the CIA, and I'm at the mall

00:39:00.040 --> 00:39:04.680
all one day just shopping with my wife and I ran into another FBI agent from

00:39:04.680 --> 00:39:08.520
Peckstead and I said hey whatever happened to those collarbone soap bills

00:39:08.520 --> 00:39:14.080
and he said oh boy he said it's just like the final scene in Raiders of the

00:39:14.080 --> 00:39:18.400
Lost Ark they boxed them up and they sent them to a storage facility in

00:39:18.400 --> 00:39:23.520
suburban Maryland he said human eyes will never see them again so here we are

00:39:23.520 --> 00:39:29.720
all these years later worried about San Bernardino worried about Paris and we

00:39:29.720 --> 00:39:33.720
You may have Taliban sympathisers living all over the United States.

00:39:33.720 --> 00:39:34.720
Wow.

00:39:34.720 --> 00:39:36.600
SBI really dropped the ball on that.

00:39:36.600 --> 00:39:38.720
And here they are collecting all our data.

00:39:38.720 --> 00:39:39.720
Exactly.

00:39:39.720 --> 00:39:41.420
They're not the terrorists.

00:39:41.420 --> 00:39:43.320
Why did you resign from the CIA?

00:39:43.320 --> 00:39:44.320
Was it ever torture?

00:39:44.320 --> 00:39:49.640
You know, I think I'm probably one of the very few people in the United States who,

00:39:49.640 --> 00:39:53.840
when I say that I'm resigning to spend more time with my children, I actually meant

00:39:53.840 --> 00:39:56.600
that I was resigning to spend more time with my children.

00:39:56.600 --> 00:40:03.400
I had gotten divorced and my ex-wife and my two sons, our two sons, moved back to Ohio

00:40:03.400 --> 00:40:07.040
to be near her parents and they were little at the time.

00:40:07.040 --> 00:40:11.280
They were seven and four and they need their dad nearby.

00:40:11.280 --> 00:40:16.240
And I knew I was going to have to go back to Pakistan or Afghanistan or Iraq or any

00:40:16.240 --> 00:40:21.280
number of terrible places and I just decided that it wasn't worth it.

00:40:21.280 --> 00:40:27.280
It was better to be with my sons than it was to be in the CIA.

00:40:27.280 --> 00:40:30.780
And so I applied for a position in a private firm.

00:40:30.780 --> 00:40:33.280
It wasn't a big form of global accounting firm.

00:40:33.280 --> 00:40:38.780
Delighted to and got a job that allowed me to work mostly over the internet.

00:40:38.780 --> 00:40:41.780
And so I could spend every other weekend with my sons.

00:40:41.780 --> 00:40:46.280
I'm proud to say that in 11 years I never missed a single weekend with them.

