00:43:40.360 --> 00:43:43.040
Do you want to tell us the Richard Welch story?

00:43:43.040 --> 00:43:45.880
Yeah, the reason why I was so interested in Greek terrorism

00:43:45.880 --> 00:43:48.400
and the reason why I went to Greece

00:43:48.400 --> 00:43:50.840
was to work on the murder case of Richard Welch.

00:43:50.840 --> 00:43:56.200
Vic Welch was the CIA's station chief in Assam in 1975

00:43:56.200 --> 00:43:59.120
and on December 23rd, 1975,

00:43:59.120 --> 00:44:02.440
he attended a Christmas party at the ambassador's residence.

00:44:02.440 --> 00:44:08.160
his wife and driver had left the party and had come back to their own home. It was the

00:44:08.160 --> 00:44:13.760
old days, you know, 1975 where there were no automatic gates. So the driver parked the

00:44:13.760 --> 00:44:19.480
car and got out of the car to open the gate and then drive the car onto the driveway. When

00:44:19.480 --> 00:44:25.200
he got out of the car, so three men and a woman got out of a car that was parked

00:44:25.200 --> 00:44:30.920
across the street. One of them shouted Welch's name. So both Mr. and Mrs. Welch

00:44:30.920 --> 00:44:35.880
got out of the car and one of the Greeks said, Richard Welch, you have been found guilty of crimes against

00:44:35.880 --> 00:44:40.760
the Greek people and you have been sentenced to death. And then shot him four times in the chest

00:44:40.760 --> 00:44:48.840
with a .45 caliber semi-automatic handgun and killed him instantly. That was the first assassination

00:44:48.840 --> 00:44:54.520
by a group that became known as revolutionary organization 17 November. And what had he

00:44:54.520 --> 00:45:00.040
done? John, had he done anything? No, in fact, he had just arrived in Greece. He was a great

00:45:00.040 --> 00:45:05.160
friend to the Greek people. He had a degree in the classics. He was fluent in ancient Greek.

00:45:05.160 --> 00:45:11.640
He was educated in archaeology and antiquities. He really loved Greece and he loved Greece. He

00:45:11.640 --> 00:45:16.840
had just arrived in the position. He hadn't done anything. So was it the position or did they

00:45:16.840 --> 00:45:21.400
have a particular personal grudge against him? No, it wasn't against him. It was against the CIA.

00:45:21.400 --> 00:45:27.480
You see, Greece was under a military dictatorship, quite a brutal one from 1967 to 1974.

00:45:27.480 --> 00:45:35.480
The military dictatorship fell in 1974, and Constantine, kind of my least, a great statesman

00:45:35.480 --> 00:45:40.840
of modern Greek history, returned to Greece from Paris and became prime minister and then

00:45:40.840 --> 00:45:46.640
held free elections, and democracy returned to the country, but 17 November, which was

00:45:46.640 --> 00:45:52.600
a very hardcore Stalinist organization, interestingly enough, decided on its own to seek revenge

00:45:52.600 --> 00:45:55.880
against what they described as enemies of Greek people.

00:45:55.880 --> 00:46:03.240
And that was Americans, British, French, Turks, and anybody associated with El Rizzo.

00:46:03.240 --> 00:46:10.160
Miss Paper Publishers, Economists, Bankers, anybody associated with the prior regime.

00:46:10.160 --> 00:46:13.160
And especially the prior regime's leadership.

00:46:13.160 --> 00:46:17.680
So they killed Welch first, and then a few months later they killed a man who had been

00:46:17.680 --> 00:46:21.280
the chief of the Greek National Police during the dictatorship.

00:46:21.280 --> 00:46:28.200
They continued killing people, 28 in all, until 2002, when the group was finally cracked.

00:46:28.200 --> 00:46:32.920
And through all those years, they did most of their assassinations with the same gun

00:46:32.920 --> 00:46:35.120
that they used to kill Dick Welch.

00:46:35.120 --> 00:46:36.120
Wow.

00:46:36.120 --> 00:46:37.120
So what was the outcome?

00:46:37.120 --> 00:46:44.120
Well, in 2002, one of the members of 17 November was carrying a bomb in a paper bag.

00:46:44.120 --> 00:46:49.760
He was carrying the bomb to the port of Piraeus where he intended to kill a major

00:46:49.760 --> 00:46:50.760
ship owner.

00:46:50.760 --> 00:46:55.760
The bomb went off in his hands and when the ambulance arrived, he believed he was dying

00:46:55.760 --> 00:46:57.760
and so he confessed to everything.

00:46:57.760 --> 00:47:04.760
And he told the ambulance attendant and the police the location of 17 November's secret weapons cache,

00:47:04.760 --> 00:47:08.760
the names of all the other members of 17 November, he gave him everything.

00:47:08.760 --> 00:47:10.760
And then he lived.

00:47:10.760 --> 00:47:12.760
The Greeks actually saved his life.

00:47:12.760 --> 00:47:15.760
He blew his hands off and he blew his right eye out.

00:47:15.760 --> 00:47:17.760
But he actually lived.

00:47:17.760 --> 00:47:24.880
the greek police raided all these different sites they arrested just about everybody if not everybody

00:47:24.880 --> 00:47:31.360
in 17 november accept the lookout in the welch assassination it was a woman and nobody was ever

00:47:31.360 --> 00:47:37.680
able to identify her pretty much everybody else was arrested including the two shooters of welch

00:47:37.680 --> 00:47:43.440
and the driver of the getaway car so where does this man live now the guy with no hands you

00:47:43.440 --> 00:47:45.440
Do you think he would be easy to find?

00:47:45.440 --> 00:47:50.440
We're serving 1,650 years in putting on us prison in Western Athens.

00:47:50.440 --> 00:47:52.440
And the woman, we don't know where she is.

00:47:52.440 --> 00:47:55.440
No, we don't know even who she is.

00:47:55.440 --> 00:47:58.440
We have some suspects, but we were never able to prove anything.

