00:51:15.960 --> 00:51:21.320
Sure. I left Athens in the summer of 2000. I went back to headquarters to work first on

00:51:21.320 --> 00:51:27.080
17 November from the headquarters side and then after September 11th I volunteered repeatedly

00:51:27.080 --> 00:51:31.800
to go to Afghanistan. My Arabic was very good at the time and I thought I was a natural to

00:51:31.800 --> 00:51:35.560
go to Afghanistan. Instead they sent me to Pakistan as the Chief of Counterterrorism

00:51:35.560 --> 00:51:43.000
operation. So I was there through much of 2002 and then I returned in the summer and

00:51:43.000 --> 00:51:47.560
went to the summit with Rodney Group. I was there very briefly and then was promoted and

00:51:47.560 --> 00:51:53.020
named the executive assistant deputy director. And in that capacity, we worked on the Iraq

00:51:53.020 --> 00:51:58.120
War, which was just a debacle from the very beginning. And the crazy thing is that there

00:51:58.120 --> 00:52:03.560
was a real fight in government over the Iraq War. There was a very clearly drawn line

00:52:03.560 --> 00:52:10.480
between the two sides. The CIA thought the Iraq War was insanity, as did the State

00:52:10.480 --> 00:52:15.820
department and the Joint Chiefs of Staff. Nobody wanted to fight this war, nobody wanted

00:52:15.820 --> 00:52:20.820
to launch it in the first place. But on the other side was the National Security Council

00:52:20.820 --> 00:52:26.140
headed by Consulisa Rice, the Office of the Secretary of Defense, OSD, that was Donald

00:52:26.140 --> 00:52:30.260
Rumsfeld, and OVP, the Office of the Vice President, Dick Chady. They're the ones

00:52:30.260 --> 00:52:33.980
who made the decision and there was to be no discussion. And so we went to war

00:52:33.980 --> 00:52:36.020
with the Rock for no good reason.

